        "original_id": "57cf6149-dc79-5401-a65b-742267745afb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dziga Vertov, Frederic Zelnik\n- Films: Lullaby (1937 film)\n- Roles: documentary film director, newsreel director, cinema theorist, producer-director, actor\n- Topics: Soviet documentary film, German silent cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Frederic Zelnik was born on 17 May 1885 and died on 29 November 1950.\n- Dziga Vertov, born David Abelevich Kaufman and also known as Denis Kaufman, was born on 2 January 1896 and died on 12 February 1954.\n- Frederic Zelnik was one of the most important producer-directors of German silent cinema.\n- Frederic Zelnik also appeared on screen as an actor.\n- Dziga Vertov was a Soviet pioneer documentary film director, newsreel director, and cinema theorist.\n- The 1937 Soviet documentary film Lullaby was directed by Dziga Vertov.",
